index ff82c3b..66b5f98 100644
--- a/doc/FPVIEW.md
+++ b/doc/FPVIEW.md
@@ -11,7 +11,8 @@ smoothly between them. **F4** cycles the views, also in **F1 > Display > Domain
 Each press swoops the camera to the next view in under a second (height, distance, tilt,
 field of view and rotation blend together; the overhead view's squashed tile rows unsquash
 on the way). The choice is saved as `domain_view` in `settings.ini` (0..3); `--fpview`
-starts in first person. **F10** turns ceilings on and off.
+starts in first person. **F10** turns ceilings on and off. **Smooth turning** (F1 > Display,
+on by default, `smooth_turns`) eases the camera and the beetle round when it turns.
 
 ## Controls in the 3D views
 
@@ -41,6 +42,10 @@ before, and the PS1 matching build is untouched: every change is inside `#ifdef
   pivot over the beetle, a distance back from it, yaw, pitch, projection, tile-row depth and
   fog (`Stg40FpPose`); a transition blends the pose it started from into the live target
   pose, eased. Classic settled: the retail renderer and camera, untouched.
+- **Smooth turning**: the camera yaw and the beetle's drawn rotation (`Stg40_FpDrawHeading`)
+  ease toward the game's heading, 20% of the way left each frame (`FP_TURN_EASE`). The game's
+  own heading, turn timing and move logic are untouched. Off: the original snap (the camera
+  at the game's 0x100 a frame).
 - **Battle exits and floor changes**: `Stg40_FpReset` (each floor set-up) drops any transition;
   the camera snaps to the chosen view at its next use. The overlay reload after a battle
   resets this state too.
